WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:02.400
AJA HAMMERLY: Managed
instance groups

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.066
are handy when you
need several VMs that

00:00:04.066 --> 00:00:05.290
are configured identically.

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:07.790
To create an instance template,
start in the Compute section

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:09.400
on the cloud console.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.370
Click Instance templates,
Create Instance Template.

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:15.460
Name your template.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.850
Pick a machine type.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.236
Update the boot disk if
you need to, and configure

00:00:20.236 --> 00:00:21.860
the rest of the
options in the way that

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:23.790
works for your project.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.730
This process is nearly
identical to setting up

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:29.040
a single instance.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.340
Be sure to check the
Allow HTTP Traffic

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.915
and Allow HTPS Traffic
Boxes if you need to.

00:00:34.915 --> 00:00:37.040
There are additional options,
including the ability

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:41.330
to add an SSH key in the
collapsed section here.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:42.194
Now, click Create.

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:48.780
To use this template,
you select it in the list

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:51.190
and you click Create
Instance Group.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.790
I hope you found this
Cloud Minute helpful.

